      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that's a solid, professional start. It's definitely better to be safe than sorry with the tone.\n\nActually, I just looked at the dashboard for the QA tool, and it's flagging your draft because the positivity score is really low—like, almost neutral. My manager is actually pushing for us to \"brighten up\" the interface across the whole app to improve brand perception, even in error states. \n\nCan you try a second version? I still want it to be professional and not a total joke, but try to find a way to bump that positivity score up a bit so it doesn't get stuck in the manual review queue. Just make it feel a bit more \"encouraging\" or \"supportive\" without being obnoxious.",
